    description: "FOUND 2026-10-03 while fixing WI-kibah / WI-kugap (branch jgstern-agent/fix/kibah). The same position-blind family as WI-bopiv, in the TYPE half: _extract_go_var_types keys a variable's type by (enclosing function name, variable name) and the FIRST binding wins, so a receiver or a method-value operand is typed from the first binding of its name anywhere in the function, not the one in scope at the use.\n\nLive (kibah branch 5e60e3ea7d; the call arm behaves the same on dev):\n\n    func F(x bool) {\n        if x { h := &A{}; reg(h.Serve); h.Serve() }\n        else { h := &B{}; reg(h.Serve); h.Serve() }\n    }\n\n-> both branches bind A.Serve (function_reference_arg and ast_call); the else branch is B.Serve.\n\nThe scope model that answers \"which binding is in scope here\" now exists: _GoLocalScope (go.py, WI-bopiv) records each local's byte range. FIX SHAPE (not built): key var_types by binding (name + scope range) and look a name up by position, as _GoLocalScope.binds does; _go_last_binding already reads the latest binding at or above a line for the handle-kind readers.\n\nNOT MEASURED: frequency on the corpus (needs a per-site comparison of the first vs the in-scope binding's type)."  # bc42
    fields: {}  # bc42
